## Evidence convention

- **Source-reviewed** means a separate reviewer inspected the recorded immutable input; it is not an executed test or peer result.
- **Focused execution** applies only to the receipt's source, test selection, fixture identities and environment. `candidate-core-asan-01` passed 44 tests; it is not complete R3 sanitizer qualification.
- **Independent peer evidence** identifies the actual independently implemented decoder/protocol endpoint and unchanged bytes it consumed. Header adaptation, patched diagnostic decoders and separately written synthesis are disclosed as narrower diagnostics.
- **Historical** entries under `Evidence/R3/`, `historical-2b2d79a/` and `historical-67c8f7e/` retain their original source/binary/environment identities. Their old complete-suite counts and claims of readiness do not apply to the takeover candidate. Failed, skipped and unavailable receipts are preserved.

At feature publication, exact receipts are copied under `Evidence/R3/codex-takeover/` with a hash index. The original source/receipt index for this checkpoint is the takeover workspace `work/` manifests and `validation/<run>/command.json`, `source-before.json`, `source-after.json`, `result.json`, and `native.log`. Review reports and matching hash manifests identify the exact reviewed subsets. At publication, preserve those identities and compact receipts with an inspectable retrieval route to full logs; do not substitute the branch name or rejected base commit for the uncommitted candidate tree.

## Primary specification scope

| Area | Pinned authority and boundary |
| :--- | :--- |
| JP3D | ITU-T T.809 (05/2011), ISO/IEC 15444-10:2011: Annex A marker syntax, Annex B packet organisation, Annex C entropy coding, Annex D transforms. |
| HTJ2K | ITU-T T.814 (06/2019), ISO/IEC 15444-15:2019: CAP/MAGB, cleanup, SigProp, MagRef and HT-set semantics. A combined Part 10+15 claim requires combined-profile evidence. |
| Part 2 high precision | ITU-T T.801, ISO/IEC 15444-2: CBD/MCT/MCC/MCO marker syntax and Annex J array synthesis. Exact integer arithmetic does not turn an irreversible-array marker into a reversible-array marker. |
| Core reconstruction | ITU-T T.800: whole-sample-symmetric transforms and inverse quantisation. Incomplete reversible coefficient precision permits reconstruction-policy choices; the diagnostic must align that policy before comparing samples. |
| JPIP | ITU-T T.808 (12/2022) V2, ISO/IEC 15444-9: Annex A data-bin framing, Clause C request/cache model, Clause D.3 EOR, Annex F HTTP/1.1. This implementation does not claim the newer HTTP/3 profile. |
| WebSocket | RFC 6455 transport carrying the repository's explicit JPIP extension. The extension is not an ITU-T T.808 WebSocket binding. A generic WebSocket implementation alone is not the required extension peer. |

